2680:## 41. Preserve loopback-only network exposure
2681-
2682-All internal services should remain bound to loopback unless an explicit product feature requires otherwise.
2683-
2684-Automated tests should fail if internal service listeners unexpectedly bind to all interfaces.
2685-
2686----
2687-
2688:## 42. Preserve navigation isolation
2689-
2690-The current URL policy correctly distinguishes the local application origin from merely similar URL prefixes. Every new WebView host must preserve this principle.
2691-
2692-Test:
2693-
2694-- correct local origin;
2695-- user-info URL tricks;
2696-- case variants;
2697-- alternate schemes;
2698-- `file:`;
--
2705:## 42A. Port-conflict termination safety
2706-
2707-Treat port-conflict recovery as a privileged operation, not a convenience helper. Security review must verify:
2708-
2709-- listener identification cannot be spoofed into killing an unrelated process;
2710-- generic names (`python.exe`, `node.exe`, `surreal.exe`) are insufficient ownership evidence;
2711-- verified runtime paths are canonicalized before comparison;
2712-- path comparisons handle case, links/reparse points, and normalization correctly on the target OS;
2713-- PID reuse/TOCTOU is mitigated by identity revalidation immediately before termination;
2714-- user confirmation cannot be bypassed in normal interactive operation;
2715-- diagnostic rendering treats process names/paths/command lines as untrusted text;
--
2722:## 43. Secrets handling
2723-
2724-Do not expose secrets through:
2725-
2726-- browser bundles;
2727-- command-line arguments when avoidable;
2728-- logs;
2729-- diagnostics reports;
2730-- crash dumps more than necessary.
2731-
2732-Review whether native Windows credential facilities can improve storage of any long-lived sensitive values without breaking portability requirements.

